+//  - each 32-bit word that changes is replaced with a compare-and-swap against the value this merge
+//    was made from; when the game changed that word in the meantime the merge is made again from the
+//    new value. (The game's own read-modify-write of a word cannot be made atomic from here; this
+//    only closes the window on the decoder's side.)
+void XmaContext::StoreContextMergedAtomic(const XMA_CONTEXT_DATA& data,
+                                          const XMA_CONTEXT_DATA& initial_data,
